--- a/docs/kamal-deployment.md
+++ b/docs/kamal-deployment.md
@@ -75,6 +75,21 @@ After the first deploy is done, any subsequent steps won't need to do that initi
 bin/kamal deploy
 ```
 
+### Configuring web push notifications
+
+To offer device notifications in notification settings, provide a VAPID key pair as
+`VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` and `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY` to both the web app and background job
+processes. For Kamal, add both names to `env/secret` in `config/deploy.yml` and
+their values to `.kamal/secrets` (or your secret manager). Never commit the private key.
+
+Keep the same key pair across servers and deployments. The public key is sent to
+the browser; the private key stays on the server and signs outgoing pushes.
+Without both keys, web push is disabled and tray/email notifications continue as usual.
+
+Web push requires HTTPS, a supported browser, and a running background job worker.
+Users enable it for each device from **Notification Settings**. On iOS, users must
+first add Fizzy to their Home Screen; the settings page includes browser-specific help.
+
 ### Configuring file storage (Active Storage)
 
 Production uses the local disk service by default. To use any other service defined in `config/storage.yml`, set `ACTIVE_STORAGE_SERVICE`.
